raditional-knowledge-and-practices-for-the-making-and-consumption-of-cassava-bread-02118"},{"name":"Remezcla, New York City's Garifuna community preserves its rich culture through food","url":"https://remezcla.com/features/culture/garifuna-food-culture-new-york-city/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-casabe"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casabe"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Taíno heritage foodways","cuisine/taino-heritage-foodways"],["Garifuna foodways","cuisine/garifuna-foodways"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Cassava","ingredient/cassava"]]}]},"dish/kanuchi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kanuchi","n":"Kanuchi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cherokee foodways","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A ",["Cherokee","cuisine/cherokee-foodways"]," soup made from hickory nuts. The nuts are dried near the stove for a month or more, cracked, and pounded shell and all into soft balls that hold together with their own oil, which are kept frozen until it's time to cook."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Cherokee Phoenix, Hickory nuts mean kanuchi","url":"https://www.cherokeephoenix.org/health/hickory-nuts-mean-kanuchi/article_fdebe40b-9b48-5849-bf6a-1601baaecbc7.html"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kanuchi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanuchi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cherokee foodways","cuisine/cherokee-foodways"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cherokee Tribal Food Distribution Program","ref":"site/food-ebci-nsn-gov","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"food.ebci-nsn.gov","note":"Traditional recipes from the Eastern Band of Cherokee Indians, like Three Sisters stew and chestnut bread.","url":"https://food.ebci-nsn.gov/?p=4673","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Cherokee foodways","links":[["Frybread","dish/frybread"]]}]},"dish/tejate":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tejate","n":"Tejate","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Zapotec foodways","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A cold drink of ",["nixtamalized","ingredient/nixtamalization"]," corn, toasted ",["cacao","ingredient/theobroma-cacao"],", mamey seeds and rosita de cacao flowers, ground to a dough and worked by hand with water until pale curds float on top. It's made mostly by ",["Zapotec","cuisine/zapotec-foodways"]," women in Oaxaca's Central Valleys and served in painted gourd bowls, with as much syrup as you like."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Roads & Kingdoms, A hundred ladies stirring chocolate drinks","url":"https://roadsandkingdoms.com/2016/hundred-ladies-stirring-chocolate-drinks/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tejate"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tejate"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Zapotec foodways","cuisine/zapotec-foodways"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Theobroma cacao","ingredient/theobroma-cacao"]]},{"h":"More from Zapotec foodways","links":[["Mole","dish/mole-sauce"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Masa","ingredient/masa"]]}]},"cookbook/the-food-of-argentina":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/the-food-of-argentina","n":"The Food of Argentina","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Ross Dobson and Rachel Tolosa Paz, 2018","square":true,"suggested":true,"isbn":"9781925418712","intro":[["Everyday Argentine cooking from asado and empanadas to sweets."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://smithstreetbooks.com/?p=1427","label":"Publisher or book page"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine"]]}]},"cookbook/mandarin-food-and-cooking-75-regional-recipes-from-beijing-and-northern-china":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/mandarin-food-and-cooking-75-regional-recipes-from-beijing-and-northern-china","n":"Mandarin Food and Cooking: 75 Regional Recipes from Beijing and Northern China","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Co